Date: 2026-08-02
Type: Feature -- recall binds, and matches on the contract rather than the name
Request-or-TODO: PIPE-050, PIPE-051, PIPE-051a
Outcome: Recall used to list names that happened to match and oblige nobody.
  Every contract now leaves recallKnownAtoms with a decision: reuse, naming the
  matching function, its artifact and the contract hash that matched it, or
  write, carrying a justification. bindRecallDecisions fails the stage naming
  any contract left undecided, which is what makes it binding.
  The match is now a contract hash -- SHA-256 over the name-erased parameter and
  result type vector, ReturnsError, and sorted deduplicated effects -- replacing
  a substring search for "func <name>(" that found a renamed atom never and a
  same-named different atom always.
  The signature-shape key exists and is deliberately incapable of a verdict: it
  is read in exactly one place, to produce a candidate count for a write
  decision's prose. Similarity can narrow, and structurally cannot admit
Affected-behavior: The recall stage can now fail. A contract with no decision is
  a stage failure rather than a silent omission
Compatibility-or-migration: The contract hash lives in a new
  internal/retrieval/recallkey package rather than internal/retrieval, because
  that package's own gate test fails the build if it imports internal/atomdoc --
  a guard protecting the M21 discovery gate, whose purpose this mechanism does
  not share. The guard was run before and after to confirm that reading
Verification: Proven to discriminate by replacing the contract-hash lookup with
  a name-only key, reproducing the exact prior defect: the rename test and the
  same-name-different-contract test both failed with those symptoms, then passed
  again on revert. TestAUDIT026 passes unmodified, confirming the vector branch
  is untouched
Known-limitations: Recall still runs after assembly and the tests, so it reports
  on code already written; moving it means restructuring Run, whose file was
  held by another lane, and StageRecall keeps its unestablished marker honestly.
  PIPE-051b stays blocked: AUDIT-026's miss measurement cannot run without a
  reviewed real-run fallback, and none exists. No end-to-end reuse is
  demonstrated, because the registry is empty until PIPE-048 lands
