Change-ID: CL-20260802-068
Commit: pending
Date: 2026-08-02
Type: Feature -- work is judged against what the run changed
Request-or-TODO: PIPE-111, PIPE-111a, PIPE-112, PIPE-113, PIPE-114, PIPE-115,
  PIPE-116
Outcome: Four gates judged the whole repository rather than the run's own
  changes, so on a repository with existing code a run touching one function was
  held answerable for every declaration in every file it opened. Attribution is
  derived from the base revision in the durable worktree binding, and
  completeness, anti-patterns, complexity, simplification, mutation and coverage
  are all scoped to it.
  A worse defect was found on the way: every check enumerated produced files
  through git status --porcelain, which sees only uncommitted edits. The moment
  a run commits to its own worktree -- the documented operating mode -- that
  went completely blind rather than merely over-broad
Affected-behavior: The six rescoped checks report on the run's own work. Each
  fails toward inclusion when attribution cannot be established
Compatibility-or-migration: None. PIPE-115's unestablished marker is cleared
  because the scoping defect it named is fixed; the gate's "branch coverage"
  wording against a statement-coverage measurement is recorded as a pre-existing
  gap rather than silently conflated
Verification: Every test carries an explicit contrasting run -- unestablished
  attribution, or a constructed wide-open attribution simulating the old
  file-level scoping -- and asserts the defect reproduces on the same fixture
  before asserting the fix. PIPE-116's twelve-function fixture repository with a
  real pre-existing anti-pattern and completeness gap is what makes the rest
  believable: a clean-slate fixture has nothing pre-existing to disagree about
Known-limitations: Zero attribution and failed attribution are distinguished by
  an explicit flag rather than by an empty map, and the fail-open direction is
  deliberate -- under-attributing would silently shrink what every gate examines
