Change-ID: CL-20260802-067
Commit: pending
Date: 2026-08-02
Type: Feature -- skip-audit stage
Request-or-TODO: PIPE-042
Outcome: A new stage 39 audits every stage this run recorded as skipped or
  not-implemented and reports the ratio, so a run cannot read as thorough while
  having declined most of its checks.
  The classification is the substance. A stage that can never satisfy and is
  named in Section33Resolved is a principled decline carrying its governing
  ticket; one that can never satisfy and is not named is no-check-by-design; a
  stage that could satisfy and recorded skipped declined after examining this
  run's own facts; the same stage recording not-implemented is unimplemented.
  Satisfied, failed and blocked are counted but not classified, because a failed
  check ran and a blocked stage was never given a fair chance
Affected-behavior: One further stage in the flow. Declared report-only in the
  refinement gates, because every row it audits is either an honest decline or a
  gap nobody has built, and a send-back would ask the work to repair the flow's
  own gaps -- a run could raise its ratio only by declining less honestly
Compatibility-or-migration: Appended as stage 39 rather than renumbered;
  PIPE-045 owns renumbering
Verification: Three discrimination proofs, each by breaking the guarded code:
  the Section33Resolved lookup, the empty-ledger guard, and the nil-store
  branch. Computed from the rows this run wrote, never from the flow
  declaration, and an unreadable ledger records skipped rather than a zero-value
  pass
Known-limitations: Not yet called from the run. The one-line wiring in
  agent_execution.go is held back because that file was contended, so stage 39
  currently records not-implemented -- honest, if incomplete
