Outcome: ci.yml is now the main gate and runs only on main and on pull requests
  into main. Its six jobs plus CodeQL's "Analyze Go" are the seven required
  checks, and their names are unchanged, because the ruleset matches required
  checks by exact job name and a renamed job becomes a required check that never
  reports and blocks every merge while looking correct. A header on the file now
  says so. dev-pass.yml is new: lint, generate-check, unit tests, and build on
  one Ubuntu runner, on dev and on pull requests into dev. It gates nothing --
  the dev ruleset requires no checks -- and its job name is deliberately
  distinct so it can never be mistaken for a required one. Each of its steps
  runs even after an earlier one failed, so a single push reports everything
  broken rather than only the first thing, and it writes a step summary saying
  in as many words that it is not a verdict. Both workflows gained
  workflow_dispatch for manual reruns
Affected-behavior: The full four-platform matrix no longer runs on every push to
  every branch, so feedback on dev is one runner instead of six. Platform-
  specific breakage is now caught at the pull request into main rather than
  earlier, which is the intended trade
